1
00:00:05,000 --> 00:00:10,486
Twenty four episodes. From auction to footprint, from delta to risk.

2
00:00:10,936 --> 00:00:16,970
Today we put it all into one trade. And we will show a losing trade too, honestly.

3
00:00:17,420 --> 00:00:20,006
This is the final episode of the series.

4
00:00:21,006 --> 00:00:25,917
Hello, this is episode twenty four of the SPIDER Order Flow series.

5
00:00:26,366 --> 00:00:33,368
Last time: risk management. Where the stop goes, how big the size, and when not to trade.

6
00:00:33,818 --> 00:00:37,057
Today, that same checklist from start to finish.

7
00:00:38,057 --> 00:00:43,203
Gold futures. Yesterday's value area was 2650 to 2672.

8
00:00:43,653 --> 00:00:47,441
Today the market opened at 2645, below yesterday's value.

9
00:00:47,891 --> 00:00:53,612
Context: an attempt to break out of balance to the downside. We look for sells.

10
00:00:54,612 --> 00:01:04,643
Morning levels: yesterday's VAL 2650, today's VWAP 2648, yesterday's low 2634.

11
00:01:05,093 --> 00:01:11,048
The plan: if price rallies to 2650, we watch whether sellers defend it.

12
00:01:12,048 --> 00:01:16,960
Price reached 2650. 1,200 contracts were bought at the ask.

13
00:01:17,410 --> 00:01:22,817
But price stayed stuck between 2650 and 2652. Sellers were absorbing.

14
00:01:23,267 --> 00:01:30,817
Then delta minus 800, and stacked bid imbalances from 2649 to 2647. Confirmation.

15
00:01:31,817 --> 00:01:40,488
Entry 2648. Stop above both the absorption high and VAL, at 2653.5.

16
00:01:40,939 --> 00:01:46,660
Risk 5.5 points. Size the usual way, 1 percent of the account.

17
00:01:47,110 --> 00:01:52,439
Target yesterday's low, 2634. Fourteen points, about 2.5R.

18
00:01:53,439 --> 00:01:59,395
Price moved down 1R, to 2642.5. We moved the stop to entry.

19
00:01:59,845 --> 00:02:03,893
Now this trade cannot lose; at worst it breaks even.

20
00:02:04,344 --> 00:02:09,020
Target 2634 hit. Plus 14 points, so 2.5R.

21
00:02:10,020 --> 00:02:17,987
Next day, same checklist, same kind of setup. Entry 2649, stop 2654.5.

22
00:02:18,436 --> 00:02:25,046
But this time price gave two half-hour closes above 2650. Acceptance above.

23
00:02:25,495 --> 00:02:32,027
Stop hit, minus 1R. That is all. The plan kept the loss small.

24
00:02:33,027 --> 00:02:37,076
The process was the same in both trades. The result was different.

25
00:02:37,525 --> 00:02:43,716
Do not judge by one trade. Look at a hundred trades to see if the method works.

26
00:02:44,716 --> 00:02:53,076
Now the whole series in a minute. Module one: auction, bid and ask, the order book, aggressive and passive.

27
00:02:53,525 --> 00:03:02,930
Module two: the truth about volume, volume profile, VWAP, session profiles, and TPO.

28
00:03:03,380 --> 00:03:11,817
Module three: the tape, footprint, delta and CVD, divergence, imbalance, absorption.

29
00:03:12,817 --> 00:03:20,367
Module four: liquidity pools, icebergs and spoofing, trapped traders, failed auctions.

30
00:03:20,817 --> 00:03:27,817
Module five: the practical setup, top-down, risk management, and today's full trade.

31
00:03:28,817 --> 00:03:32,787
What next? First practice on replay, then a demo account.

32
00:03:33,238 --> 00:03:41,833
Write every trade in a journal: context, level, confirmation, and result. Check the numbers after fifty trades.

33
00:03:42,283 --> 00:03:46,722
And to test your method with data, watch our Quant series.

34
00:03:47,722 --> 00:03:50,963
Thank you for staying with us for twenty four episodes.

35
00:03:51,412 --> 00:03:57,055
If the series helped, subscribe to the channel and share the playlist with friends.

36
00:03:57,505 --> 00:04:02,912
Our Telegram and Instagram are in the description. See you with a new topic.

